  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>From Gigaro beach, the coastal path enters the Domaine du Cap Lardier, a Conservatoire du littoral site where scrubland and coves offer views of Cap Taillat and the Îles d'Or. The La Croix-Valmer tourist office describes an 8.22 km loop (282 m of elevation gain, orange level, fairly difficult): the outward leg goes through the scrubland, the return along the coastal path. "Les 2 Caps", which push on to Cap Taillat, cover 13 km (about 5 h).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Dogs are accepted in the Domaine du Cap Lardier, on a leash only, as the coastal path is narrow (Port-Cros and Porquerolles National Park, tourist office). On beaches, they may only go onto them to cross, and they are prohibited on beaches in summer. In summer, access to the massif is regulated from 21 June to 30 September depending on fire risk (prefectoral order). The terrain is rocky and exposed: bring water. Gigaro car park is paid from 1 June to 30 September, 9am to 7pm.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: bring plenty of water, avoid the hottest hours and check your dog's paw pads at the end of the walk.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>La Croix-Valmer and its beaches are close by, and Cap Taillat offers one of the finest viewpoints on the Var coast.</p>
